1
00:04:41,052 --> 00:04:47,052
The sun never sets on vengeance.

2
00:09:22,105 --> 00:09:28,105
Catch the Bullet is a western, action film directed by Michael Feifer.

3
00:14:03,157 --> 00:14:09,157
marshal Britt MacMasters returns from a mission to find his father
wounded and his son kidnapped by the outlaw Jed Blake.

4
00:18:44,210 --> 00:18:50,210
Hot on their trail, Britt forms a posse with a
gunslinging deputy and a stoic Pawnee tracker.

5
00:23:25,263 --> 00:23:31,263
But Jed and Britt tread dangerously close to the Red Desert’s Sioux territory.

6
00:28:06,315 --> 00:28:12,315
Britt MacMasters, played by Jay Pickett.

7
00:32:47,368 --> 00:32:53,368
Sheriff Wilkins, played by Peter Facinelli.

8
00:37:28,421 --> 00:37:34,421
Dex, played by Tom Skerritt.

9
00:42:09,473 --> 00:42:15,473
Chad, played by Mason McNulty.

10
00:46:50,526 --> 00:46:56,526
Jed Blake, played by Gattlin Griffith.

11
00:51:31,578 --> 00:51:37,578
Chaska, played by Cody Jones.

12
00:56:12,631 --> 00:56:18,631
Lost Bullet (French: Balle perdue) is a 2020 French action thriller film directed by Guillaume Pierret, written by
Guillaume Pierret, Alban Lenoir and Kamel Guemra and starring Alban Lenoir, Nicolas Duvauchelle and Ramzy Bedia.

13
01:00:53,684 --> 01:00:59,684
It was Pierret's first feature film.

14
01:05:34,736 --> 01:05:40,736
Lost Bullet tells the story of an auto mechanic forced to go on the run
and battle corrupt police officers when framed for murder.

15
01:10:15,789 --> 01:10:21,789
The action relies heavily on practical stuntwork and effects.

16
01:14:56,842 --> 01:15:02,842
A Netflix production, the film was released globally on June 19, 2020.

17
01:19:37,894 --> 01:19:43,894
It became a streaming hit and received generally
favorable reviews, launching a franchise.

18
01:24:18,947 --> 01:24:24,947
A sequel, Lost Bullet 2, was released in 2022, and a third
film, Last Bullet, was released in 2025.
